/></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Evidence for the intracellular location of chloride channel (ClC)-type proteins: co-localization of ClC-6a and ClC-6c with the sarco/endoplasmic-reticulum Ca2&#x0002b; pump SERCA2b.</article-title><source>Biochem J</source><volume>330</volume><issue> Pt 2</issue><fpage>1015</fpage><lpage>1021</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9480924</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000474-Buyse2"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Buyse</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Voets</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Tytgat</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>De Greef</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Droogmans</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>Expression of human pICln and ClC-6 in Xenopus oocytes induces an identical endogenous chloride conductance.</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><volume>272</volume><fpage>3615</fpage><lpage>3621</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9013613</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000474-Voets1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Voets</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Buyse</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Tytgat</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Droogmans</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Eggermont</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>The chloride current induced by expression of the protein pICln in Xenopus oocytes differs from the endogenous volume-sensitive chloride current.</article-title><source>J Physiol</source><volume>495</volume><issue> Pt 2</issue><fpage>441</fpage><lpage>447</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8887755</pu